# XCU vi
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# vi is a screen editor whose input and output must be a terminal; with
# other devices the behaviour is not defined by the page, so the whole page
# is recorded as untestable.

assertion  XCU.vi.001
anchor     utilities/vi.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/vi.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/vi.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      untestable
since      1992
says       vi edits the named files in a screen on the terminal, with the
           -c, -r, -R, -t and -w options and the visual-mode commands, and
           writes the buffer to a file only by an editor command.
reason     The behaviour is defined for a terminal that shows screens and
           sends keystrokes; with standard input or output not a terminal
           the page defines nothing, and a script has no terminal to supply.
